.in 5
.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
strip
- remove the symbol table from a linked image
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
strip file ...
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Strip removes the symbol table from each Whitesmiths image named.  The
image's header is rewritten with a zero symbol table size and the file
is cut down to header, text and data, so the symbols no longer occupy
space on the disk.
.sp 2
A file that is not a linked image - a relocatable object, an archive,
or an ordinary text file - is left alone, so strip can be handed every
program in a directory and only the runnable ones come back smaller.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
NOTES
.in +5
.br
The kernel must not be stripped: its overlays live in its own file and
the symbol table is part of what it opens.  Strip the userland
instead, which is where the space matters.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
ar (1), ld (1), nm (1), size (1)
